The next step is to select Menu 3. The wall is
Surface type 1, the ceiling is surface type 2, and the
floor is surface type 3. The final DHC is 2751
Btu/ F, indicating that the room surfaces will store
and return 2751 Btu for each 1°F of sinusoidal. room
temnerature swing.

To complete the calculation of aT(swing}, we need
to know Qs, the daily transmitted solar radiation
per ft2 of direct gain glazing. At 40° latitude,
this {s about 1440 Btu/ft2 per day. A is 30 ft2,
Therefore, using Eq. (5):

aT(swing) = (0.61)(1440)(30)/(2751) ,
aT(swing) - 9.6°F

This is the peak-to-peak temperature swing to be
expected on a clear winter day.

